      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if your symptoms seem mild, the combination of widespread hives and throat tightness is a medical red flag that could indicate a severe allergic reaction progressing quickly. Relying on more antihistamines alone after doubling a dose does not eliminate the risk of anaphylaxis or the danger of choking if swelling worsens while you sleep. It is much safer to leave the ER or urgent care immediately, as they are far better equipped to handle a potentially life-threatening situation than waiting to see what happens.",
